Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe-specific]

The meta-aws patch 001-set-cmake-min-version-for-external-project-sdk-and-src-path
redirects ExternalProject_Add for the SDK to use OE's pre-fetched source tree.
However, it also removes the empty CONFIGURE/BUILD/INSTALL/TEST commands and adds
CMAKE_ARGS. This turns the ExternalProject from a source-locator into a full
configure+build step that lacks OE's CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE, causing cross-compilation
ABI detection to fail.

The actual SDK build happens via add_subdirectory() in the main CMakeLists.txt,
which inherits the toolchain. ExternalProject just needs to locate the source.

Restore the no-op commands so ExternalProject only unpacks the source dir without
attempting to configure or build.

Index: aws-iot-device-client-1.10.1/CMakeLists.txt.awssdk
===================================================================
--- aws-iot-device-client-1.10.1.orig/CMakeLists.txt.awssdk
+++ aws-iot-device-client-1.10.1/CMakeLists.txt.awssdk
@@ -6,5 +6,8 @@ include(ExternalProject)
 ExternalProject_Add(aws-iot-device-sdk-cpp-v2
         SOURCE_DIR              "${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/../aws-iot-device-sdk-cpp-v2-src"
         BINARY_DIR              "${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/aws-iot-device-sdk-cpp-v2-build"
-        CMAKE_ARGS             -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5
+        CONFIGURE_COMMAND       ""
+        BUILD_COMMAND           ""
+        INSTALL_COMMAND         ""
+        TEST_COMMAND            ""
         )
